WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.137 --> 00:00:05.638
[door opening]

00:00:05.705 --> 00:00:07.173
[exhales]

00:00:11.845 --> 00:00:15.882
Francis, there is an
Englishman waiting for you.

00:00:15.949 --> 00:00:17.016
These tables are no good.

00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:18.184
No good at all.

00:00:18.251 --> 00:00:19.519
He is from the
Hudson Bay Company.

00:00:19.586 --> 00:00:21.121
I gave Lafarge
exact measurements.

00:00:21.187 --> 00:00:22.689
A table that will
not tilt or list.

00:00:22.756 --> 00:00:24.791
That is all I ask for, a
proper table, but this--

00:00:24.858 --> 00:00:27.794
We will deal with the
table at the proper time.

00:00:27.861 --> 00:00:29.028
There is a man.
He is wanting--

00:00:29.095 --> 00:00:30.130
I said not now, Mathilde.

00:00:38.104 --> 00:00:39.706
You have ruined my refinement.

00:00:39.773 --> 00:00:40.940
Now what will we do?

00:00:41.007 --> 00:00:42.876
We don't have money for
these refinements, Francis!

00:00:45.578 --> 00:00:48.982
It is the floor that
is tilt, not the table.

00:00:49.048 --> 00:00:51.217
I advised against
green wood planks,

00:00:51.284 --> 00:00:53.019
but did you heed my advice?

00:00:53.086 --> 00:00:54.421
No.

00:00:54.487 --> 00:00:56.689
Everything here is poor
and broken and made wrong.

00:00:56.756 --> 00:00:57.957
Even this.

00:00:58.024 --> 00:01:00.960
It is no use.

00:01:01.027 --> 00:01:05.865
These are unrefined tables
to serve unrefined food

00:01:05.932 --> 00:01:07.734
for unrefined men.

00:01:07.801 --> 00:01:10.670
That is our business, Francis.

00:01:10.737 --> 00:01:12.572
[footsteps approaching]

00:01:14.441 --> 00:01:17.544
A minute is a
minute, not five.

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:18.344
My apologies.

00:01:18.411 --> 00:01:19.712
My husband and I were just--

00:01:19.779 --> 00:01:23.583
Discussing refinements.

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:24.451
After a room?

00:01:24.517 --> 00:01:25.185
HAMISH: Aye.

00:01:25.251 --> 00:01:26.686
Two, actually.

00:01:31.191 --> 00:01:34.093
He is my equal and will
be treated as such.

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:37.530
I have the other
guests to consider.

00:01:37.597 --> 00:01:40.733
I wish to be civil
in all enterprises,

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:44.571
but I will not be denied a
proper room for my co-equal,

00:01:44.637 --> 00:01:46.773
Yvon.

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:48.541
Though he can speak for himself.

00:01:48.608 --> 00:01:49.342
YVON: Aye.

00:01:49.409 --> 00:01:51.344
He is deadly with that book.

00:01:51.411 --> 00:01:53.012
I am not his equal in that.

00:01:53.079 --> 00:01:54.981
My apologies.

00:01:55.048 --> 00:01:56.716
We will ready the rooms.

00:01:56.783 --> 00:01:57.517
Thank you.

00:02:10.063 --> 00:02:11.831
Mathilde Geffard.

00:02:11.898 --> 00:02:13.233
Aye, Mathilde.

00:02:13.299 --> 00:02:16.870
I wish to know about a
recent guest in your inn.

00:02:16.936 --> 00:02:22.175
My husband keeps very careful
records of all the guests.

00:02:22.242 --> 00:02:23.376
HAMISH: Well, then.

00:02:23.443 --> 00:02:26.513
I am looking for a
Mr. Randall Cross.

00:02:26.579 --> 00:02:28.781
That name is not
familiar to me.

00:02:28.848 --> 00:02:30.950
HAMISH: He was an agent
for the Hudson Bay Company.

00:02:31.017 --> 00:02:35.288
His correspondence indicate
that he was a guest at your inn.

00:02:35.355 --> 00:02:38.491
He describes the
food as adequate,

00:02:38.558 --> 00:02:42.962
though he did have a few words
of praise for the prune tart.

00:02:43.029 --> 00:02:45.632
Exceptional, he wrote.

00:02:45.698 --> 00:02:46.933
It can be, on occasion.

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:49.369
We would like to see the
room Mr. Cross stayed in.

00:02:49.435 --> 00:02:51.771
Well, first I must check
to see if he was a guest.

00:02:51.838 --> 00:02:52.705
Francis--

00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:54.340
Stay out of this.

00:02:54.407 --> 00:02:56.943
Aye, Mr. Cross was a guest.

00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:58.945
He stayed in the Rose Suite.

00:02:59.012 --> 00:03:00.513
He left us some time ago.

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:02.081
I just wanted to
make sure before--

00:03:02.148 --> 00:03:04.050
I am sure.

00:03:04.117 --> 00:03:07.453
These men do not have
time for games, Francis.

